{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/922077-new-storyteller-here","id":922077,"title":"New Storyteller Here","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-27T10:33:54-07:00","id":922077,"title":"New Storyteller Here","content":"Hey everyone,<br /> So I kind of recently got into CoD and I'm interested in running a game for some of my friends. I've never actually run a game before but I really like the setting and the system seems pretty straightforward. I was wondering though if anyone had any advice for a new storyteller like me?<br /> <br /> The plan for the initial game is to use a modified version of the Wake the Dead adventure in the core book, however, just to make it a little sadder and more interesting for my players, I want to keep Lucien McJack as a normal person who just comes back from the dead, as opposed to a demon possessed monster or whatever he is. I'm hoping having to decide whether or not to kill an innocent man, who they were responsible for killing in the first place, will lead to some fun drama. I'm also keeping the mirror vulture character as a connection to the God-Machine, but I will not have a lot of direct connections or clues to the existence of the god-machine in this adventure. They'll just come to realize that a bird like creature is searching for someone come back from the dead and that it is really bad if that person gets found. The primary enemies they will be fighting will be like zombies who have gone rabid and possibly at some point, the mirror vulture himself.<br /> <br /> So tell what you guys think and let me know if you have any suggestions, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,"